   },
   {
    "itemId": "ENG-006-TM-04",
    "district": "ENGLISH",
    "optionValue": "He drops the hammer on somebody's toes.",
    "seatTag": "en-wrong-scope-retrieval",
    "sourceFile": "eng006draft (5).json",
    "sourceDigest": "ff3b82e08cf3c9e9",
    "THE_TEXT_IN_THESE_ROWS": "True of line 48, but that is much later, at the first blow. In the window, line 18 answers the stem: 'And then he would lift up the picture, and'.",
    "itsSha256": "a4f4716d9bf63a7437d6561cec3bec9d2c4b5a5dff5d01707af006f762b22009",
    "THE_TEXT_IN_THE_CROSSED_ARTEFACT": "True of line 48, but that is much later, at the first blow.",
    "itsSha256Crossed": "c8f979e928467e13dfc2a812d561dce673d11226d8f577ebf3dbe594fcdacfcc"
   },
   {
    "itemId": "ENG-006-TM-04",
    "district": "ENGLISH",
    "optionValue": "He drops it and the glass stays whole.",
    "seatTag": "en-plausible-not-stated",
    "sourceFile": "eng006draft (5).json",
    "sourceDigest": "ff3b82e08cf3c9e9",
    "THE_TEXT_IN_THESE_ROWS": "Lines 18 and 19 have him try to save the glass and cut himself on it. A glass that survives is a real-world outcome those lines never state.",
    "itsSha256": "1e16d48c51a40ec4ec03a2e1793503e3cd106851370a63ff4585e14be2a212e7",
    "THE_TEXT_IN_THE_CROSSED_ARTEFACT": "Line 19 says he tries to save the glass and cuts himself on it.",
    "itsSha256Crossed": "69842d7ab6c8171e92d99ab4bacc6719f637bce52bdbfe21c04340643482d215"
   },
   {
    "itemId": "ENG-006-TM-08",
    "district": "ENGLISH",
    "optionValue": "A line drawn on the wall to work from.",
    "seatTag": "en-wrong-scope-retrieval",
    "sourceFile": "eng006draft (5).json",
    "sourceDigest": "ff3b82e08cf3c9e9",
    "THE_TEXT_IN_THESE_ROWS": "Reuses the mark on the wall from line 34; the rule is a separate thing he takes up. In the window, line 38 answers the stem: 'down. And he would take the rule, and re-measure'.",
